# LF everywhere, in the working tree as well as in the index.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `tools/build-index.mjs --check` compares the bytes it would generate
# against the bytes on disk, and it generates LF. On a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` -- which
# is the setting on the machine this repo is developed on -- a checkout would rewrite every file
# to CRLF, and that check would then report drift on a clean tree while passing in CI, where the
# runner has no such setting. A check that fails only on the author's machine is a check that
# gets switched off.
#
# It also matters for what this repo is: the trail files are read by software, on whatever
# platform. A byte-for-byte stable file is the point.
* text=auto eol=lf
